--- The centity it's attached to, or `nil`.
---@return Centity?
function BossBar:attached() end

--- Takes it off every screen for good.
---@return boolean # `false` once it's gone already.
function BossBar:remove() end

--- The panel of lines at the right of one player's screen, from `player:sidebar()`: up to 15 lines of MiniMessage under a title, without the score numbers vanilla shows. Setting its title or lines shows it. A sidebar needs a scoreboard of the player's own, so while it shows NetherForge gives them one that copies the server's teams and the lines under name tags (the project's own changes at once, anyone else's within a second), keeping team colours and name tags working; hiding it gives them the server's back. It's cleared when they leave. For someone offline its methods answer `nil` or `false`.
---@class Sidebar
local Sidebar = {}

--- Its title, as MiniMessage, or `nil` when it has none (or they're offline).
---@return Text?
function Sidebar:title() end

--- Changes its title, and shows it.
---@param text Text MiniMessage.
---@return boolean # `false` when they're offline.
function Sidebar:set_title(text) end

--- Its lines, top first, as MiniMessage. Empty when it has none (or they're offline).
---@return Text[]
function Sidebar:lines() end

--- Replaces its lines, and shows it. More than 15 is an error.
---@param lines Text[] MiniMessage, top first. Lines may repeat; an empty string is a blank line.
---@return boolean # `false` when they're offline.
function Sidebar:set_lines(lines) end

--- Whether they see it now. `false` when they're offline.
---@return boolean
function Sidebar:is_visible() end

--- Shows it, or hides it and gives them the server's scoreboard back, keeping its title and lines for next time.
---@param visible boolean
---@return boolean # `false` when they're offline.
